Message-ID: <c3c978dd2382c25a61799440c6e891b42af5a9de.1792019330.git.claude@p7x.dev>
From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] claude/skills/freebsd-port: Justify every Makefile line
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: wqqrqzuyotnrtrxltpxlvwspqkooryto
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:08:55 +0000

Lines copied from other ports or from upstream's build without a
reason end up in the patch and cost a review round to remove. The
signoz port stamped a git hash that only fed a log line, because
upstream's Makefile does; the release version already identified the
source. Each such line is also one more thing to keep right on every
update.

Ports in the tree stay the place to look for ideas, but each line
that goes into the Makefile now needs a purpose toward a working
package.
---
change-id: wqqrqzuyotnrtrxltpxlvwspqkooryto
base-branch: b/dev@upstream

 .claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md | 8 ++++++++
 .claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
index 96d47cb..5b2ce91 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
@@ -104,6 +104,14 @@ A port is `Makefile`, `distinfo`, `pkg-descr`, and a plist
 (`pkg-plist`, `PLIST_FILES`, or one the framework generates). Keep the
 Makefile in the order the handbook gives.
 
+Every line of the Makefile must serve the outcome, a package that
+builds and works. Other ports are a source of ideas, not of lines to
+copy. Before keeping a variable, know what reads it and what breaks
+without it; if nothing does, leave it out. A git hash stamped beside
+a release version is one such line, since the version already
+identifies the source. When a line's purpose is not obvious, say why
+it is there in the patch notes.
+
 - Take dependency bounds from upstream's own list (`Cargo.toml`,
   `go.mod`, `pyproject.toml`, `mix.exs`) and express them in
   `*_DEPENDS`. Where the tree cannot satisfy a bound, loosen it to what
diff --git a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org
index 72c9bc5..6eedfb4 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org
+++ b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 - create a new port from user provided info, or update an existing
   port
 - research ports tree for similar ports to determine patterns
+  - do not cargo cult: every line in the Makefile must be there to
+    support a working package; take ideas from other ports, not lines
 - look at upstream / dist sites etc to use the latest good version
   - newest released version from release page or registry, not just tags
   - exclude yanked versions

